; A standalone interval allocator: given a script of allocations and frees
; (keys and sizes only), it places every block at an offset in one pool so
; that blocks live at the same time never overlap, and it can prove a
; placement correct with its own witness check. It knows nothing about
; tensors, kinds or Bigarrays: units are the client's, and the client makes
; one problem per pool. See .ai/ (the tensor arena design).
;
; Depends on [err_trace] and [fmt] only, so `dune build lib/interval_alloc`
; proves the boundary. It is reachable from js_of_ocaml, hence sizes and
; offsets are [int64] throughout: nothing here assumes a 63-bit [int].
;
; Wrapped (default): consumers see [Interval_alloc.Script] and so on. The
; [Ia_*] modules are the implementation behind the one public module.

(library
 (name interval_alloc)
 (private_modules
  ia_check
  ia_decode
  ia_reference
  ia_script
  ia_search
  ia_solution
  ia_strategy)
 (libraries err_trace fmt))
